WEBVTT

00:43:29.384 --> 00:43:30.654
Corey, what do you think?

00:43:31.091 --> 00:43:34.194
Have you got any other questions there
before we wrap up?

00:43:34.924 --> 00:43:36.385
CH: No, I think we're good,

00:43:36.409 --> 00:43:38.903
I mean, I think
we're going to get through it,

00:43:38.927 --> 00:43:40.474
I guess is what we're saying,

00:43:40.498 --> 00:43:43.260
but we also have an opportunity here

00:43:43.284 --> 00:43:46.436
to make some changes and do better
and emerge stronger.

00:43:46.460 --> 00:43:47.673
And as you said,

00:43:47.697 --> 00:43:50.697
take a look at things
and the structures that we have in place

00:43:50.721 --> 00:43:52.348
and see where we can improve,

00:43:52.372 --> 00:43:56.791
but it's going to take
a collective action and cooperation.

00:43:57.894 --> 00:43:59.711
CA: Yeah, Ray, I'm definitely inspired

00:43:59.735 --> 00:44:04.077
by the actions that you're taking
as a philanthropist